# Build context of docker/ssam-server/Dockerfile: the SSAM tree without history, local state, build outputs or secrets.
# Every file this context keeps ends up in the image (COPY . /app, plus what the build stages compile from it), so the
# guard platforms/odc/facade/tests/hosted-image-denylist.test.mjs reads exactly this set against the client names of
# docker/ssam-server/client-denylist.json (owner rule of 2026-10-07: client content may ship, client NAMES may not).
.git
**/.git
.claude
**/.claude
**/.local
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/TestResults
**/__pycache__
*.user
*.credentials.json
.ssam-local.json
.env
**/.env
**/tokens.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
.dockerignore

# ---- what .gitignore keeps out of the repository stays out of the image too: Studio captures, lab work, journals
platforms/odc/lab
platforms/odc/snapshots
platforms/odc/journal
platforms/odc/output
platforms/odc/tmp
platforms/odc/.backup-*
**/*.oml
**/*.oap
**/*.osp
# the job bases the image serves: the neutral fixtures and the anonymized ODC lane fixture (with their sidecars)
!kernel/tests/fixtures/*.oml
!kernel/tests/fixtures/odc/blank-*.oml
!kernel/tests/fixtures/odc/insurance-reactive-r8.oml
kernel/tests/fixtures/odc/*.json
!kernel/tests/fixtures/odc/blank-*.oml.json
!kernel/tests/fixtures/odc/insurance-reactive-r8.oml.json

# ---- the publisher's lists and release tooling (the client list itself never ships)
docker/ssam-server/client-denylist.json
scripts/release
platforms/odc/tenants.json

# ---- not run by the hosted server: tests, benches, evidence and the history of the work on client modules
tests
docs/evidence
agent/tests
platforms/odc/tests
platforms/odc/facade/tests
platforms/odc/portal/tests
platforms/odc/portal/research
platforms/odc/docs
!platforms/odc/docs/model-api
platforms/odc/jobs
platforms/odc/studio/builder/smoke-*
kernel/docs/proofs
kernel/docs/specs
kernel/docs/tasks
kernel/docs/mapa
kernel/tests/Anvil.*
kernel/tests/Shared
kernel/tests/SSAM.*
kernel/tests/RuntimeConnect
kernel/tests/*.py
kernel/tests/archive
kernel/tests/access
kernel/tests/jobs-live
kernel/tests/jobs-cold
kernel/tests/jobs-coverage
kernel/tests/jobs-coverage-f2
kernel/tests/fixtures/hmisjha
kernel/tests/fixtures/flow-layout-*.json
kernel/docs/PROVAS.md
kernel/docs/GITSSAM-O-QUE-SE-APROVEITA.md
kernel/docs/architecture/2026-09-04-arquitetura-produto.md
kernel/scripts/base_cache_check.py
kernel/scripts/outsystems_padroes/tests
platforms/odc/portal/*.md
# the developers' history in docs/ (the hosted server reads docs/CONHECIMENTO-DO-TIME.md and serves the coverage
# matrices docs/COBERTURA-EXEMPLOS-*.md; it reads nothing else there)
docs/COBERTURA-DESCOBERTA-FASE1.md
docs/DEBUGGER-*.md
docs/HANDOFF-*.md
docs/FASE2-AGENTE.md
docs/LAYOUT-MOTOR.md
docs/LOTE-DADOS-FASE3.md
docs/MEDICAO-VELOCIDADE.md
docs/MIGRACAO.md
docs/O11-BRIDGE-FINA.md
docs/OPERACOES-O11.md
docs/PILOTO-FASE2.md
docs/PACOTE-*.md
docs/proofs
# work done for clients: its scripts, html sources and browser contracts carry the client in the file name
kernel/scripts/*dcips*
kernel/tests/html/dcips-*
kernel/tests/browser/dcips-*
kernel/tests/ui/dcips-*
# Windows-only credential prompts of the Portal lane (the hosted server runs no Windows prompt)
platforms/odc/portal/runtime/*.ps1
# the ODC Studio bridge runs in the customer's Studio, never in the hosted server (the image does not build it)
platforms/odc/studio/bridge
# the builder's features are the owner's lab and the logic of client apps; a hosted customer delivers jobs, not features
platforms/odc/studio/builder/features
# compose secrets (NGROK_AUTHTOKEN): never inside the image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# the Studio installers come in through their own build context (installers), read by the studio-* stages only
docker/installers

# ---- added by the SSAM-MCP monorepo (not from the server line): its production image and deploy run outside the image.
# Dockerfile (production) and deploy/ (compose, Caddyfile, runbook, backup scripts, and the operator's .env and any
# archive left there); state archives of deploy/backup.sh anywhere in the tree (customer data and customer names).
Dockerfile
deploy
**/ssam-state-*.tar.gz
**/ssam-state-*.tar.gz.*
